# ai/AGENTS.manifest — concat order for ~/.codex/AGENTS.md build
# One file per line, paths relative to ~/.config/ai/. Comments via `#`.
# feedback_ai_config_structure.md MUST be the first memory entry (carries token substitution).

# Top-level metas
PERSONAL.md
guardrails.md

# Rules (alphabetical by topic)
rules/code-review.md
rules/diagnostics.md
rules/pager.md
rules/portability.md
rules/rationalization.md
rules/testing.md

# Memory (config-structure rules first — enables all later tokens)
memory/feedback_ai_config_structure.md
memory/feedback_no_guessing.md
memory/feedback_prompt_format.md
memory/feedback_reverse_grep.md
memory/feedback_rule_removal_backtrace.md
memory/feedback_code_review_per_commit.md
memory/feedback_raw_urls.md
memory/feedback_memory_english.md
memory/feedback_global_memory_path.md
memory/feedback_pager_poll_during_long_turns.md
memory/feedback_commit_message_style.md

# Private memory is deliberately absent: memory/private/ is gitignored, so naming
# a file here makes this tracked manifest reference a path that only one machine
# has, and every other machine reports it as drift on every commit. The builder
# and the drift check still handle memory/private/* entries (codex/scripts/
# bootstrap.sh skips a missing one, claude/scripts/sync-back.sh resolves one
# against the main checkout from a worktree) — that path is for a private entry
# added on purpose, not for pinning one machine's files into the shared list.
